# Scene tree as source of truth

Prefer Godot scene hierarchy over invisible script-only wiring. Someone should be able to click a node in the dock and understand where a system starts.

## Do

- Put **real entrypoints** on authored scene nodes (script + children that own the work).
- Nest collaborators under that node so the tree shows the pipeline (e.g. `VoiceSpellValidator` → `SpellValidationRunner`).
- Keep **one** owner per job — no mirror/copy nodes that duplicate the same listener or service.
- Use child nodes for **session contracts / settings** when they are the authored truth (e.g. `VoiceSession/Listeners/Chat`), and update those nodes in place for live status.

## Don't

- Add empty stub nodes that only hold a flag while all logic lives elsewhere.
- Spawn runtime mirror trees (e.g. `Listening/*` clones of `Listeners/*`).
- Hide primary call chains only in autoloads/match scripts when a Match/GameApp node should own them.

## Examples in this project

- Good: `Match/VoiceSpellValidator` owns STT prepare + `start_validation`; runner is its child.
- Good: `GameApp/.../VoiceSession/Listeners/Chat|Spellcasting` are the only listener nodes; broker updates them in place.
- Bad: a node whose script is only `var use_stub := false` with no API.
- Bad: broker creating parallel `Listening/Chat` copies of authored listeners.
